{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Its produce.</b> Also what you bring in to it — as in what is written: ״זְרַעְתֶּם הַרְבֵּה וְהָבֵא מְעָט״ (Haggai 1) (Sifrei)." "<b>And you will perish quickly.</b> For all the other afflictions — I will exile you from the land that caused you to sin. A parable: a king who sent his son to a banquet and sat and instructed him: do not eat more than you need, so that you come home clean. But that son paid no heed; he ate and drank more than he needed, and vomited and soiled all the banqueters. They seized him by his hands and feet and threw him behind the palace (there)." "<b>Quickly.</b> I give you no extension. And if you say: but was not an extension given to the generation of the Flood, as is written, ״וְהָיוּ יָמָיו מֵאָה וְעֶשְׂרִים שָׁנָה״ (Genesis 6) — the generation of the Flood had no one from whom to learn, but you have someone from whom to learn (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:34.801578100Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}